This project bundles third-party binaries under different licenses. The MIT
license above applies to Retrarr's own source (retrarr.sh, build_db.sh, docs,
etc.). Bundled binaries carry their own upstream licenses:

  - bin/aria2c-mister  — GPL v2 (from aria2 upstream, GNU aria2 project).
                         License text: LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt
                         Source: https://github.com/aria2/aria2
                         Static build source:
                         https://github.com/abcfy2/aria2-static-build

  - bin/chdman-mister  — GPL v2 (part of MAME).
                         License text: LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt
                         Source: https://github.com/mamedev/mame
                         Static build source:
                         https://github.com/emmercm/chdman-js
                         (when bundled — not present in every branch)

The combination is "mere aggregation" under GPL v2 §2: the GPL-licensed
binaries and the MIT-licensed script coexist in a distribution without one
license infecting the other. If you redistribute Retrarr with these binaries,
you must honor GPL v2's obligations for the binaries (include the license
text, point to source, no additional restrictions on the binaries themselves).
